Package: tidyepidemio
Title: Tidy Tools for Epidemiologic Analysis
Version: 1.1.0
Authors@R: person("Jimmy", "Moses", email = "jimmy.moses@pnguot.ac.pg", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Data-first tools for descriptive and analytic epidemiology, simple
    causal standardization, infectious disease dynamics, surveillance, spatial
    scanning, preprocessing, and forecast evaluation. Provides explicit estimands and transparent
    implementations for exploratory analysis.
URL: https://github.com/jmozez/tidyepidemio
BugReports: https://github.com/jmozez/tidyepidemio/issues
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: cli, dplyr, ggplot2, rlang, tibble, vctrs, recipes,
    rsample, yardstick, generics, parsnip, tidyselect, stats, utils, survival
Suggests: testthat (>= 3.0.0), roxygen2, knitr, broom, hardhat
Config/testthat/edition: 3
Roxygen: list(markdown = TRUE)
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.1.1
